{
 "version": 1,
 "_comment": "Player weapons. Every weapon is built from the same TEMPLATES (the fists' moves) scaled by the weapon's numbers, so adding or retuning a weapon means changing a handful of numbers, not 10 moves. speed < 1 is faster (it scales the wind-up and recovery frames). reach scales how far the blow reaches (hit box offset and length), width how wide it is in the lane, power the damage, knockback how far the target is pushed, launch how high it is knocked up, stun how long it is stunned, stamina what the moves cost. 'overrides' then replaces any field of any single move with an absolute value: this is where each weapon gets the flavor of its run and jump attacks (knockback, launch, stun or plain damage). Generated move ids are <weapon>_<template>, for example sword_run_heavy. skill_names are the names shown in the brush-stroke banner when the special skill or ultimate is used.",
